---
const layers = ['Frontend', 'Backend', 'Data', 'Commerce', 'Integrations', 'DevOps', 'Infrastructure']
const projects = [
  { number: '01', title: 'Movix', type: 'PRODUCT PLATFORM', text: 'A fast, editorial movie discovery experience with rich APIs, smart filters, and a visual browsing rhythm.', tags: 'React · Redux · REST API', href: 'https://movix-site.vercel.app/' },
  { number: '02', title: 'H-Rent', type: 'REAL ESTATE', text: 'A focused rental platform that turns property search into a clear, confident decision-making flow.', tags: 'Next.js · Node.js · Database', href: 'https://rent-in.vercel.app/' },
  { number: '03', title: 'Embarkist', type: 'STARTUP ECOSYSTEM', text: 'A modular product ecosystem designed to help ambitious teams move from first idea to real traction.', tags: 'Strategy · Cloud · Systems', href: 'https://embarkisttesting.netlify.app/' },
]
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0a09" />
    <title>Shivam Singh — Engineer & CTO</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Shivam Singh is an engineer and CTO who owns the whole system, from product to production." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="header wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">SHIVAM RAO <span>ENGINEER & CTO</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#work">WORK</a><a href="#process">PROCESS</a><a href="#stack">STACK</a><a href="#contact">CONTACT</a></nav>
      <a class="availability" href="mailto:hello@wrkwithshivam.dev"><i></i> AVAILABLE FOR WORK</a>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 — WHAT I DO</p>
          <h1>One engineer who owns the <em>whole system,</em> not a slice of it.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Most engineers own a slice — the front end, or the API, or the infrastructure. I take the whole problem: design it, build it, deploy it, run it, and fix it when it breaks.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="mailto:hello@wrkwithshivam.dev">BOOK A CALL <span>↗</span></a><a class="underlined" href="#work">SEE THE WORK <span>↓</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="layers-panel">
          <p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOU HEAR WHEN NOBODY OWNS IT</p>
          <ol>{layers.map((layer, index) => <li tabindex="0"><b>0{index + 1}</b><strong>{layer}</strong><span>{['“The API is slow, not us”', '“It works on my machine”', '“That query has always been like that”', '“The platform will not let us”', '“That is the vendor’s SDK”', '“Nobody touches the deploy”', '“That is the host’s problem”'][index]}</span></li>)}</ol>
          <p class="panel-caption">SEVEN LAYERS, ONE OWNER</p>
        </div>
        <div class="facts"><div><span>BASED</span><strong>India, working remote</strong></div><div><span>SINCE</span><strong>2017</strong></div><div><span>STACK</span><strong>Shopify · Node · AWS · React</strong></div></div>
      </section>

      <section id="work" class="work wrap">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 — SELECTED WORK</p><p>A few systems I&apos;ve helped bring<br />from 0 → 1 and beyond.</p></div>
        <div class="projects">{projects.map((project) => <article class="project"><div class="project-visual"><span class="project-number">{project.number}</span><div class="window"><div class="window-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>product / overview</span></div><div class="window-body"><small>{project.type}</small><strong>{project.title}</strong><div class="chart"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="blocks"><b></b><b></b><b></b></div></div></div></div><div class="project-detail"><p class="eyebrow">{project.type}</p><h2>{project.title}</h2><p>{project.text}</p><span class="tags">{project.tags}</span><a class="underlined" href={project.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VISIT PROJECT <span>↗</span></a></div></article>)}</div>
      </section>

      <section id="process" class="process wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 — HOW</p><p>The method is simple.<br />The ownership is rare.</p></div><div class="process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h2>Build</h2><p>Understand the business problem, design the solution, then write the product or stand up the infrastructure myself. No handoff in the middle.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h2>Run</h2><p>Deploy it and operate it. Debugging goes from DNS through the network, the server, the container and the application into the database.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h2>Optimise</h2><p>Measure what it actually costs — in load time, server bills, and hours lost to manual work — fix that, and measure again.</p></article></div></section>

      <section id="stack" class="stack wrap"><p class="eyebrow">04 — STACK</p><div class="stack-content"><h2>The tools change.<br /><em>The principles don&apos;t.</em></h2><div class="stack-list"><span>React / Next.js</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>Node.js</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>AWS / Vercel</span><span>System design</span></div></div></section>
      <section id="contact" class="contact wrap"><p class="eyebrow">05 — LET&apos;S TALK</p><div><h2>Have a good<br /><em>problem?</em></h2><div class="contact-copy"><p>Tell me what you&apos;re building, where you&apos;re stuck, or what could be better. I&apos;m always interested in thoughtful work with ambitious people.</p><a class="email" href="mailto:hello@wrkwithshivam.dev">hello@wrkwithshivam.dev <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top">SHIVAM RAO <span>ENGINEER & CTO</span></a><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} · BUILT WITH INTENTION</span><div><a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GITHUB ↗</a><a href="https://linkedin.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LINKEDIN ↗</a></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,500;1,500&display=swap');
